</fo:list-item>
</fo:list-block>
</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always" space-after="0.4em">
<fo:block font-weight="bold" font-style="normal" keep-with-next="always">Senior Engineer</fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always">
<fo:inline font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">
	Level 3 Communications, LLC
      </fo:inline> (Louisville, Colorado)</fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">May 1998–Present</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block provisional-distance-between-starts="0.5em">
      Responsible for Engineering and Software Development to support
      Level 3's national network.  This includes automatic configuration
      of routers and switches, DNS, NTP, DHCP and other IP services.
    </fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always" space-after="0.4em">
<fo:block font-weight="bold" font-style="normal" keep-with-next="always">Director</fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always">
<fo:inline font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">
	Sprint Paranet (formerly Paranet)
      </fo:inline> (Dallas, Texas)</fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">October 1997–May 1998</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block provisional-distance-between-starts="0.5em">
      Responsible for the definition of services to be offered by Sprint
      and Sprint Paranet in their new Remote Operations Center.  Provide
      technical and managerial leadership to the team that will
      implement the defined services.  Provide vision for Sprint and
      Sprint Paranet's Remote Operations Center.  Personally involved
      with the Remote Operations Center since its inception, including
      project definition, project planning and presentations.
    </fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always" space-after="0.4em">
<fo:block font-weight="bold" font-style="normal" keep-with-next="always">Network Design Analyst</fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always">
<fo:inline font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">Paranet</fo:inline> (Dallas, Texas)</fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">May 1993–September 1997</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block provisional-distance-between-starts="0.5em">
      Provided consulting, integration and operations support for
      Paranet and Paranet's customers. Provided support and consulting
      for the operation, design and implementation of networks. Provided
      UNIX system administration support.  Provided support for
      world-wide implementation of directory and naming systems.
      Provided specialized training in networking and naming services to
      Paranet and Paranet's customers. Contributed to the creation of
      Paranet's recruiting process, including forms and database
      development. Significant contribution to Paranet's professional
      cadre through the technical interview process.  Responsible for
      all of Paranet's IT operations for a significant period of time.
    </fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic" keep-with-next="always">Projects:</fo:block>
<fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1.0em" provisional-distance-between-starts="0.750em" space-after="0.750em">
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Naming System Design and Implementation
	  Designed and implemented an enterprise-wide implementation of
	  WINS, DNS and DHCP.  Provided custom applications to provide
	  automatic generation of DNS and WINS tables from 2 different
	  central databases. Managed the work of 3 other administrators.
	  Managed 30 Solaris UNIX servers, including world-wide
	  installation tasks. Also provided support and custom
	  applications in support of the enterprise-wide X.500 database.
	  Provided custom training covering DNS and DHCP support.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Automated Router Configuration Tracking
	  Designed and implemented custom applications that queried more
	  then 500 Cisco routers and Catalyst switches. Used a
	  combination of SNMP and other techniques to collect data.
	  Maintained databases of router configurations and reported on
	  differences from baseline.  Maintained accurate databases of
	  MAC address locations and IP addresses.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Internet Security Implementation
	  Provided security for a segment of a large electronics
	  company.  Utilized Cisco router access lists, logdaemon, tcp
	  wrappers and other utilities.  Managed the project and 12
	  administrators.  Worked closely with the segment's management
	  and corporate's security department.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Internet, Intranet and Naming Training
	  Developed and presented multiple training courses on internet
	  and intranet systems, and support of those systems. Also
	  included training for DNS and DHCP systems.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Internet Firewall Implementation
	  Provided security for a large communications company. Utilized
	  TIS firewall toolkit, Socks proxies and router access lists.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Network Management Workstation Implementation
	  Provided a SNMP management station installation for a large
	  communications company.  Utilized SunNet Manager.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Internet Mail Gateway
	  Provided Internet Mail access to a large, multi-company
	  corporation.  Provided domain name hiding to present a single
	  mail address to the internet.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>New Office Opening
	  Performed initial projects in Denver, Colorado.  Interviewed
	  candidates for Sales Manager and Technical Analyst positions.
	  Supported city for a period of 3 months.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Lotus Organizer and cc:Mail Integration
	  Integrated Lotus Organizer and cc:Mail in a Novell Netware
	  enterprise-wide network on both IBM compatible and Apple
	  Macintosh computers.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Corporate Intranet
	  Designed and implemented a nationwide intranet.  Includes 30
	  sites connected with Cisco routers utilizing Frame Relay for
	  the WAN links. Includes multiple analog dial-in servers and a
	  T1 internet connection with a TIS Guantlet firewall. 
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Fault-Tolerant Novell Netware Installation
	  Designed and implemented a fault-tolerant installation of
	  Novell Netware for a large hospital.  Utilized a NetFrame
	  400FT super-server to replace over 18 Microsoft LanManager
	  servers.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Enterprise-Wide Network Redesign and Deployment
	  Designed and help with implementation of a large,
	  multi-protocol enterprise-wide network. Banyan Vines, TCP/IP
	  and other protocols were deployed.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
</fo:list-block>
</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always" space-after="0.4em">
<fo:block font-weight="bold" font-style="normal" keep-with-next="always">Systems Analyst II</fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always">
<fo:inline font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">
	Texas A&amp;M University
      </fo:inline> (College Station, Texas)</fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">December 1988–May 1993</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block provisional-distance-between-starts="0.5em">
      Served as a primary technical support analyst. Provided support
      for all microcomputer applications on Apple Macintoshes and IBM PC
      compatibles. Provided support and programming on UNIX platforms.
      Specialized in network support and integration, including
      AppleTalk, Novell, IBM, 3-Com and TCP/IP. Cross platform
      integration was an integral part of the duties performed. Custom
      programming provided as required.
    </fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic" keep-with-next="always">Projects:</fo:block>
<fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="1.0em" provisional-distance-between-starts="0.750em" space-after="0.750em">
<fo:list-item>
<fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" start-indent=".5in">
<fo:block>•</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-label>
<fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
<fo:block>Enterprise-Wide Novell Netware Installation and Supervision
	  Designed and implemented an enterprise-wide Novell Netware
	  environment encompasing more than 140 servers and 20 sites
	  across the state of Texas.
	</fo:block>
</fo:list-item-body>
</fo:list-item>
</fo:list-block>
</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always" space-after="0.4em">
<fo:block font-weight="bold" font-style="normal" keep-with-next="always">Department Head and Manager</fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always">
<fo:inline font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">
	Texas A&amp;M University
      </fo:inline> (College Station, Texas)</fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">January 1986–December 1988</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block provisional-distance-between-starts="0.5em">
      Served as manager and department head for the University owned
      computer store. The store resold computers to the students,
      faculty, staff and departments. As manager of the center, directed
      the expansion of sales from $750,000 to more the $4,000,000
      annually.  Instrumental in bringing sales to University
      departments and the expansion of the center's product line and
      services.
    </fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always" space-after="0.4em">
<fo:block font-weight="bold" font-style="normal" keep-with-next="always">Microcomputer Specialist</fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always">
<fo:inline font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">
	Texas A&amp;M University
      </fo:inline> (College Station, Texas)</fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">June 1985–January 1986</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block provisional-distance-between-starts="0.5em">
      Served as the primary support person. Duties at the Micro Computer
      Center included technical support and responsibility for the
      assembly and testing of computers sold by the Micro Computer
      Center.  Duties at the Support Center included serving as the
      primary contact for departments having trouble with
      microcomputers.  Responsible for many different departments,
      computer models, peripherals and problems.
    </fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always" space-after="0.4em">
<fo:block font-weight="bold" font-style="normal" keep-with-next="always">Consultant</fo:block>
<fo:block keep-with-next="always">
<fo:inline font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">Small Business Systems</fo:inline> (College Station, Texas)</fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic">May 1983–June 1985</fo:block>
</fo:block>
<fo:block provisional-distance-between-starts="0.5em">
      Independent computer systems consultant and integrator.  Performed
      functions such as problem evaluation, equipment selection,
      software selection, custom software design and custom programming.
      Customers included Brazos County, Texas, the Texas Agricultural
      Extension Service as well as other government and commercial
      clients. Worked in the central Texas area from Houston to
      Killeen/Fort Hood to Waco.
    </fo:block>
<fo:block>
<fo:block font-weight="normal" font-style="italic" keep-with-next="always">Projects:</fo:block>
